# Line-ending policy.
#
# Patch files and the provenance file that records their sha256 must be
# byte-stable across checkouts: docs/hardware-decode/toolchain-provenance.json
# pins the patch hashes, and tests/hwdecode/sources.py refuses to run when a
# hash does not match. With `core.autocrlf=true` (a common Windows default,
# and the setting on the machine where v0.7.0 was authored) git re-encodes
# text files to LF at commit time, which silently changed the patch hashes
# and made `python -m tests.hwdecode.harness provenance` fail on a clean
# checkout. Force LF so the recorded hashes stay valid everywhere.
*.patch text eol=lf
